WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:03.620
At the deepest point your buddy signals: out of gas.

00:03.620 --> 00:05.540
You share, and you both go up.

00:05.540 --> 00:07.980
How much must still be in your tank for that?

00:07.980 --> 00:09.690
That is minimum gas.

00:10.790 --> 00:16.970
Minimum gas: the gas two divers need to get from the deepest point to the surface on one tank, breathing hard.

00:17.130 --> 00:18.430
Courses size it differently;

00:18.430 --> 00:20.160
the idea is the same.

00:22.460 --> 00:31.240
Our example dive, at its deepest point, twenty metres: two stressed divers at twenty litres a minute each, from an eleven point one litre tank.

00:31.240 --> 00:35.530
The way up: a minute to sort out the problem, then three metres a minute on average.

00:37.280 --> 00:41.320
Step one, the rate: twenty litres a minute each, two divers.

00:41.480 --> 00:42.380
Forty litres a minute.

00:43.560 --> 00:50.400
Step two, the pressure: three atmospheres at twenty metres, one at the surface: add them and halve.

00:50.400 --> 00:51.450
Two atmospheres.

00:53.550 --> 01:00.130
Step three, the time: twenty metres at three metres a minute, plus the minute at depth.

01:00.130 --> 01:01.620
Rounded up, eight minutes.

01:02.870 --> 01:06.970
Step four: rate times pressure times time.

01:06.970 --> 01:08.540
Six hundred and forty litres.

01:10.840 --> 01:14.760
Step five, into bar: divide by the tank's litres.

01:15.160 --> 01:19.470
Fifty-seven point seven, rounded up to sixty bar: minimum gas for this dive.

01:22.570 --> 01:28.830
Minimum gas is a floor under the plan: when either gauge gets there, the dive is over, whatever the plan said.

01:30.250 --> 01:38.130
By the deepest point, from a single aluminium eighty: forty, sixty and a hundred bar, rounded up, and never less than forty.

01:38.130 --> 01:39.860
Your course's figures come first.

01:42.960 --> 01:47.600
Turn Pressure works out minimum gas for your dive, and the turn pressure.

01:47.840 --> 01:49.760
Free on the App Store.

01:49.760 --> 01:51.390
diver dot today.
